From: Nahum Shalman <nshalman@edgecast.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Jun 2026 02:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Honor build-users-group on illumos in useBuildUsers

useBuildUsers() in src/libstore/unix/user-lock.cc gates the
build-user-switching code path in DerivationBuilderImpl::startBuild()
(src/libstore/unix/build/derivation-builder.cc:713). The function has
per-platform arms for __linux__ (autoAllocateUids + buildUsersGroup),
__APPLE__/__FreeBSD__ (buildUsersGroup only), and an #else that
unconditionally returns false. illumos falls through to #else, so even
with build-users-group set in nix.conf, builds run as root.

This bypasses the entire build-user mechanism: SimpleUserLock::acquire,
the setreuid in the child, and the chown of the build directory all
get skipped. Externally this looks like nix reading the setting (it
appears in `nix show-config`) but ignoring it.

The illumos arm matches the FreeBSD/Apple shape: SimpleUserLock is
portable (its one __linux__-only call, get_group_list for supplementary
GIDs, is already #ifdef-guarded), and autoAllocateUids is intentionally
not supported (it needs user namespaces, which illumos lacks). Add
__sun to the existing #elif arm.

After this patch, with build-users-group = nixbld in nix.conf, a
nixbld group + nixbldN users in /etc/passwd, and root invocation, the
build phase forks and setreuid's to one of the nixbld users.

---
 src/libstore/unix/user-lock.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/libstore/unix/user-lock.cc
+++ b/src/libstore/unix/user-lock.cc
@@ -227,7 +227,7 @@ bool useBuildUsers()
 #ifdef __linux__
     static bool b = (settings.buildUsersGroup != "" || settings.autoAllocateUids) && isRootUser();
     return b;
-#elif defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__FreeBSD__)
+#elif defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__sun)
     static bool b = settings.buildUsersGroup != "" && isRootUser();
     return b;
 #else
